<title>BELGIUM: AEA airlines cargo up 4.1 pct in Jan-Aug 1996.</title>
<headline>AEA airlines cargo up 4.1 pct in Jan-Aug 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Global freight traffic carried by West European airlines in the first eight months of 1996 was up 4.1 percent on the same period last year at 15.16 billion freight tonne-kilometres, FTK, the Association of European Airlines (AEA) said.</p>
<p>The FTK measurement is derived by multiplying the weight of cargo carried by the distance flown.</p>
<p>In January-August 1996, the biggest volume of traffic was transported on Europe-Far East/Australasia routes, the number of FTK flown increasing by 9.1 percent to 5.69 billion FTK.</p>
<p>Airfreight transported by AEA member airlines, by geographical region, between January and August 1996, with percentage change on January-August 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p>Traffic area January -August 1996  (in million/billion FTK)</p>
<p> Geographical Europe	   583.1million  down  1.0 pct</p>
<p> Europe/North Africa M/East  649.5million  up   15.6</p>
<p> North Atlantic		  5.45bn    down  0.8</p>
<p> Far East/Australasia	  5.69bn    up    9.1</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa	    1.23bn    up    2.0</p>
<p> South Atlantic		  878.8ml   up   10.0</p>
<p> Mid-Atlantic		    671.2million  down  2.4</p>
<p> Total longhaul		  13.92bln  up    3.8</p>
<p> Total International	   15.16bln  up    4.1</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
